{"nodes": [{"id": "craft_services_setup_index_page", "label": "Craft Setup Wizard Page", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_wizard_state", "label": "wizard state object", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "everything interactive on the page derives from `wizard` via decideWizardState()/applyWizardState(); nothing is enabled or disabled ad hoc and no control depends on a single un-retried network call. originally btn-seed shipped disabled and was only enabled by one branch of one fetch whose only error handler was console.error, so a slow container, storage timeout, or non-JSON error body left the page permanently inert with no explanation"}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_decidewizardstate", "label": "decideWizardState()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "pure branch table (no DOM, no fetch, no globals) mapping what's known about the host to what the wizard should look like; extracted for the same reason SetupGate is - the branch table is the whole behaviour and the part that broke. covered by tests/setup-wizard/"}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_applywizardstate", "label": "applyWizardState()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_statusreaderror", "label": "statusReadError()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "returns null when a /api/setup/status response is usable, else a short reason; the empty-200 case is not hypothetical - a route bound MapGet's RequestDelegate overload and wrote nothing at all, so res.ok was true, there was no Content-Type, and res.json() threw on an empty body. checking res.ok alone would not have caught it"}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_loadstatus", "label": "loadStatus()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_refreshstatus", "label": "refreshStatus()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "the initial read and the background refresh are the same operation, so a failed first attempt recovers on its own rather than bricking the page for the rest of the session"}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_seedfirstuser", "label": "seedFirstUser()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_startautomatedsetup", "label": "startAutomatedSetup()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_pollfortoken", "label": "pollForToken()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_services_setup_index_completesetup", "label": "completeSetup()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/Services/Setup/index.html", "sour